long before the marvel cinematic  universe conquered the world sam raimi  ushered in the golden age of superhero  movies courtesy of his spider-man  trilogy but will we ever see his  spider-man 4 keep watching for raymie's  answer thanks to sam raimi's  blockbusters about peter parker and his  alter ego marvel adaptation stopped  being a laughingstock following years of  ill-fated movies like howard the duck  are you nuts  the director along with star toby  maguire helped turn spidey into a bona  fide live-action star it's been smooth  sailing for superheroes at the movies  ever since naturally fans of spandex  crusaders were excited when raymie  agreed to helm doctor strange in the  multiverse of madness however now that  raymie has finally joined the mcu many  people would love to see him return to  the spider-man saga and oversee the  friendly neighborhood arachnid's next  mcu outing unfortunately raymie doesn't  envision himself cheating on his own  spider-man franchise with the current  iteration while spider-man 3 didn't  exactly blow people's minds many fans  would love to see raymie have another  crack at a spidey flick in the near  future especially after learning that he  had plans for another sequel back in the  day however the director wouldn't direct  the next tom holland lead flick if he  was offered the chance as he doesn't  want to upset his favorite spidey actor  in a recent interview with the los  angeles times raymie praised spider-man  no way home for opening up the  multiverse and bringing some of his old  friends into the fold he also had kind  words to say about the direction in  which the mcu has taken spidey with  holland in the star and role even if his  personal loyalties lie elsewhere raymie  said i love spider-man and i love tom  holland in the role but if i made a  spider-man movie it would probably have  to be with toby or he'd break my neck of  course raymie might consider returning  to the spider-man franchise if marvel  agreed to let him make a new movie with  maguire he previously told fandango i  don't know if marvel would be interested  in that right now i don't know what  their thoughts are about that i haven't  really pursued that but it sounds  beautiful even if it wasn't a spider-man  movie i'd love to work with toby again  in a different role  sam raimi had plans for a fourth  spider-man movie back in the 2000s but  that was a long time ago the hollywood  machine has continued to churn out hit  movies since then and raymie has moved  on with his life these days he doesn't  even think about spider-man 4 very often  during a recent conversation with screen  rants raymie revealed that spider-man 4  isn't at the top of his project wish  list at the moment on top of that he  doesn't even know if marvel's head  honchos are interested in resurrecting  his iteration of the franchise raymie  told the outlet i currently don't have  any plans to make spider-man 4 and  they're so successful with the new  spider-man series that i don't know if  that's gonna happen or not i haven't  pursued that still stranger things have  happened in hollywood prior to  spider-man no way home no one expected  maguire holland and andrew garfield to  play their respective spider-man in the  same movie theoretically raymie could  make spider-man 4 and it would make  sense within the context of the mcu so  never say never and if you need more  reassurances you'll be pleased to know  that a notable marvel employee wants to  see this dream become a reality grant  curtis the marvel producer whose credits  include moon knight as well as sam  raimi's original trilogy of spider-man  films believes that raymie's franchise  still has life left in it during an  interview with gizmodo from earlier this  year the producer revealed that raymie  and company came up with plenty of  material for more movies years ago so  they aren't short of ideas should  spider-man 4 ever materialize curtis  said the spider-man movies we made were  an incredible opportunity career-wise as  a fan i loved the narratives that were  generated from those three movies there  were other stories within those movies  that did not get told i hope sunday as  any spider-man fan would tell you that  all of those stories come out and that  narrative continues  curtis might only have been sharing his  personal opinion but it's good to know  that some influential people have  spider-man 4 in their thoughts it  remains to be seen if ramy gets to  finish telling the stories that he  envisioned all those years ago however  he does reportedly want to make a batman  movie and that's arguably even more  exciting than spider-man 4  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the mcu are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

